                <pb facs="0340" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">412.00/116: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-06T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">February 6,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 11:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. Department’s mail instruction number 1161 October 9, 1919.</p>
                <p>The Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs called me to the Foreign Office last
                    evening to say that the Mexican Government is now prepared to enter into an
                    arrangement for the consideration by a mixed commission of American claims
                    against Mexico and Mexican claims against the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
